From 60876c5f8fad221756afd9bbd534377b7ff06571 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hamed7ir <hamedghorbani17@live.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:02:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [ARM] Port Windows SEH support from upstream 6c34ed7b3 (PR
 #184953)

Ports __try/__except/__finally support for thumbv7-windows-msvc into the 18.1.8 tree.
45 of 53 upstream hunks apply verbatim. Three adaptations and one drop:

DROPPED: the 'NumBytes -= GPRCS3Size;' hunk. rt1 has no GPRCS3 area - 18.1.8 has a two-way
callee-save split - and rt1's patch 0001 already carries the identical correction as
'NumBytes = GPRCS2Offset;'. Applying both would under-allocate by 8 bytes.

RE-ANCHORED: three hunks whose context names post-18 symbols (t2BXAUT_RET, TCRETURNrinotr12)
or an upstream-only comment line.

ADAPTED: CLEANUPRET's pattern. Upstream writes [(cleanupret bb)] because main declares
SDTCleanupret as SDTypeProfile<0,1>; 18.1.8 declares cleanupret with SDTNone - zero operands -
so the upstream spelling fails TableGen. In-tree precedent for the 18 spelling: AArch64 and
X86 both write [(cleanupret)]. CATCHRET needs no change; 18's SDTCatchret is already <0,2>.

Test IR adapted to 18: 24 'getelementptr inbounds nuw' -> 'inbounds' (nuw on GEP is 19+),
2 'captures(none)' -> 'nocapture' (20+ spelling), and llvm.lifetime.{start,end}.p0 restored to
18's (i64 immarg, ptr) signature. 17 CHECK lines rebaselined for two assembler-PRINTING
differences - 18 prints '.set NAME, VALUE' where main prints 'NAME = VALUE', and 18
parenthesises ':lower16:(SYM)'. Every emitted VALUE is byte-identical to upstream's
expectation, verified symbol by symbol, so these are rebaselining and not findings.

wineh-framepointer.ll is untouched: its three __chkstk constants already read 1254/1256/1257
because patch 0001 produced them. That triple is the anti-double-application oracle and rt1+0009
still emits it.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5 (Anthropic)
